---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Independence & Affiliate Disclosure"
  seoTitle="Editorial Independence & Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="How Australian Home Collective uses affiliate links, protects editorial independence and reviews products before promotional placement."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Commercial relationships</p>
      <h1>Editorial Independence & Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Affiliate income supports Australian Home Collective. This page explains how commercial
        relationships affect our buying links and how we protect our editorial conclusions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="content narrow">
    <p class="small">Policy updated 14 October 2026.</p>
    <h2>How affiliate links work</h2>
    <p>
      If you make a qualifying purchase through an affiliate link, Australian Home Collective may
      earn a commission at no extra cost to you. You are free to visit a retailer directly or buy
      elsewhere; using our links is never required.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Amazon Associate statement:</strong> As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying
      purchases.
    </p>
    <p>
      Affiliate revenue helps keep our guides free and the site clean, easy to use and free from
      intrusive display advertising. We may work with additional affiliate networks, retailers or
      other commercial partners over time, but the same editorial rules apply to every relationship.
    </p>

    <h2 id="buying-link-selection">How affiliate relationships affect buying links</h2>
    <p>
      Our shopping links are limited to retailers and brands with an approved affiliate
      relationship through which AHC can earn commission. Affiliate availability therefore
      affects which retailers and products appear with buying links. Our linked selections
      cover part of the market; suitable products and retailers may exist outside those partnerships.
    </p>
    <p>
      A commercial relationship alone does not make a product suitable. Products must meet the
      research requirements for the claims we make, and we retain control over assessments,
      drawbacks and conclusions. A missing buying link does not mean that a product or retailer
      is unsuitable. Links to manuals, research and other editorial sources are separate from
      shopping links and do not require an affiliate relationship.
    </p>

    <h2>How retailer links are ordered</h2>
    <p>
      Where we list several retailers for the same product, higher-paying affiliate partners
      appear first, based on the verified commission rate applicable to that product. This affects
      the order of retailer links, not our product assessments or the editorial ranking of
      researched products. Retailer order does not indicate the lowest price or best
      delivery offer. Check each retailer's current price and terms before buying.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial independence comes first</h2>
    <p>
      AHC decides what to cover and what to conclude. Brand suggestions and commercial opportunities
      may bring products to our attention, but partners cannot require favourable coverage, remove
      material drawbacks or buy a higher editorial ranking. Popularity, price, star ratings and
      commission alone are not evidence of suitability.
    </p>
    <p>
      A product can receive promotional affiliate placement only after it meets our documented
      {" "}<a href="/how-we-select-products/">AHC Product Research</a> standard and is separately
      approved for affiliate use. The surrounding guide must remain useful if a reader does not
      use the link.
    </p>

    <h2>Research, not implied testing</h2>
    <p>
      Unless a guide explicitly states what Australian Home Collective tested and how, we have not
      personally tested the product. Our assessments are based on research, including relevant
      manufacturer and warranty documents, independent expert or technical reviews, recurring
      owner-feedback themes, Australian availability and support, and regulator or recall checks
      where relevant.
    </p>

    <p>
      We publish material drawbacks, who an option may suit, who it may not suit, the evidence
      confidence and the date of the research review. A link is not a guarantee that a product will
      suit every household.
    </p>

    <h2>Supplied products and sponsorship</h2>
    <p>
      If a brand supplies or lends a product, funds travel or provides another material benefit
      connected with coverage, we disclose that benefit in the relevant content. Sponsored content
      is clearly labelled. Neither a supplied product nor payment purchases a favourable conclusion.
      Brands can submit evidence for factual corrections, but AHC retains final editorial control.
      See our <a href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial Standards</a> for the safeguards we apply.
    </p>

    <h2>Ongoing review</h2>
    <p>
      Approved products are re-reviewed at least every 180 days and sooner when material new
      evidence emerges. A product may be downgraded, paused or removed if its specifications,
      availability, support, safety position or reliability evidence changes. Affiliate reviews
      also confirm that the exact listing still matches the intended product, remains available to
      Australian customers and retains the configured tracking; a working URL by itself is not
      sufficient.
    </p>

    <h2>Reader choice</h2>
    <p>
      You are never required to use our links. Before buying, check the retailer's current
      product information, price, delivery details, returns policy and suitability for your
      household.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
